From 89c0bd86074de7d2d40a8bfb1bf27d51ae5fabdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:58:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: align x and y by row for regression and correlation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The bridge passed x and y through numeric_column, which drops missing
values in each column separately: with gaps in different rows the pairs
shifted silently (or lengths differed and the method failed). Added
ParsedTable.aligned_numeric (NaN in place) and used it for the xy call
kind and the regression scatter plot; methods already drop incomplete
pairs. Affects simple_linear_regression, pearson_correlation and the
ch. 12–13 regression methods; regression_diagnostics now reports the
file's row numbers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A2hqwsyFif9SnDnzK8co2e
